  "steps": [
    "Soak 250g dried chickpeas (kabuli chana) overnight (8 hours). Drain and rinse well.",
    "To a pressure cooker add: the soaked chickpeas, 1 medium potato (150g), cut in half, 1 bay leaf, 1 tsp salt, enough water to cover.",
    "Pressure cook for 4-5 whistles on high heat, then bring the flame to low and cook for another 5 minutes. If you have an electric pressure cooker, 20 minutes will do (even if you’re using canned chickpeas).",
    "Now to a blender add: the cooked potato, 1 tbsp cooked chickpeas, 80g high-protein Greek yogurt, a splash of the cooker water.",
    "Blend until smooth and set it aside.",
    "To a pan on medium heat add: 1½ tbsp mustard oil, 2 finely chopped onions (200g), 1 inch finely chopped ginger (15g), 2 chopped green chillies.",
    "Cook until the onions turn golden brown (took me like 3 minutes).",
    "Now add: ½ tsp turmeric, 1 tsp red chilli powder, 2 tsp coriander powder, 1 tbsp chana masala. Mix well.",
    "Pour in the yogurt and potato mixture and cook for 3 minutes.",
    "Now add the cooked chickpeas along with some of the cooking liquid.",
    "Add: 1 tsp brown sugar, ½ tsp salt.",
    "Mix well and let it simmer for a few minutes until the gravy becomes thick and slightly mushy. (It took me about 15 minutes.)",
    "For the tadka, heat: 1 tbsp ghee. Add 2 slit green chillies, ginger juliennes (8g), 1 tsp kasuri methi, pinch of hing.",
    "Let it sizzle, then pour the tadka over the chole.",
    "Garnish with fresh coriander and your Chikkar Chole is ready!"
  ],
